&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who are we?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Ensono, our purpose is to be a relentless ally, disrupting the status quo and enabling our clients to Do Great Things. As a trusted technology adviser and managed services provider, we help clients navigate continuous change and embrace innovation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We deliver world-class transformational services across AI, hybrid cloud, infrastructure, mainframe, data, IdAM, and cloud-native solutions, simplifying complex business challenges and creating new pathways to success. Headquartered in the USA and backed by private equity, Ensono has a strong track record in the UK and Europe, with growth plans built on trusted partnerships and deep industry expertise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Business Development Executive&lt;/strong&gt;, you will play a pivotal role in accelerating Ensono’s growth in the UK by identifying, developing and converting opportunities with organisations that align to our Ideal Client Profile (ICP).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will take a proactive, insight-led approach to opening new client relationships and building a high-quality pipeline of net-new logo opportunities. Using market intelligence, targeted research and AI-enabled tools, you will identify where Ensono can add the greatest value, develop compelling account and pursuit strategies, and create actionable business development initiatives that bring our full portfolio of capabilities to the UK market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working closely with senior sales leaders, sales and wider go-to-market teams, you will help shape opportunities from initial prospect identification through to proposition and pursuit development. You will bring strong commercial judgement, curiosity and creativity, using client and market insight to turn potential opportunities into meaningful business conversations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate will be an accomplished business development professional with a strong track record of creating new opportunities and engaging senior stakeholders. You will be confident using AI and data to sharpen prospecting and account strategies, an excellent communicator, and a collaborative self-starter with the energy and commercial focus to help Ensono win new clients and deliver sustainable growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How Your Success Will Be Measured and Rewarded&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;At Ensono, we want great business development to deliver great outcomes and be recognised accordingly. Success in this role will be measured through the number and quality of leads you generate, the new-logo opportunities and pipeline you create, and your contribution to converting those opportunities into sustainable growth. You&#39;ll have clear lead-generation and pipeline objectives, with strong performance recognised and rewarded through Ensono&#39;s incentive arrangements, eligibility for Presidents Club nomination, and recognition via the global Elevate recognition platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role &amp;amp; Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Generation &amp;amp; New Logo Pipeline Development: &lt;/strong&gt;Proactively generate and qualify leads within organisations aligned to Ensono’s Ideal Client Profile (ICP), using targeted, multi-channel outreach to build a high-quality pipeline of net-new logo opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Target Account Prospecting: &lt;/strong&gt;Develop and execute focused prospecting plans across priority accounts, identifying key decisionmakers, buying signals and relevant entry points for Ensono.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner with New Logo Sellers: &lt;/strong&gt;Work closely with New Logo Sales to identify, engage and qualify prospective clients, providing insight and account intelligence that helps open doors and progress opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market Intelligence &amp;amp; Whitespace Identification: &lt;/strong&gt;Conduct targeted research across industries, markets and competitors to identify whitespace, emerging client needs and new opportunities for Ensono.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-Enabled Business Development: &lt;/strong&gt;Use AI extensively to enhance prospect research, identify buying signals, personalise outreach, develop account strategies and increase the effectiveness and scale of lead-generation activity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Target Account Management: &lt;/strong&gt;Own and continually refine Target Account Lists (TALs), prioritising activity based on market intelligence, engagement data, seller input and opportunity potential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client Engagement &amp;amp; Relationship Building: &lt;/strong&gt;Build relationships with key decision-makers and influencers, creating relevant conversations that connect client priorities with Ensono’s capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Qualification &amp;amp; Opportunity Development: &lt;/strong&gt;Qualify prospective opportunities and work with sellers to move strong leads through the early stages of the sales cycle, ensuring effective handover and continued momentum.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Propositions &amp;amp; Pitches: &lt;/strong&gt;Contribute insight and research to tailored propositions, pitches and pursuit activity that demonstrate Ensono’s value and differentiation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Go-to-Market Collaboration: &lt;/strong&gt;Work across Sales, Marketing, Alliances and solution teams to coordinate campaigns, account-based activity and market initiatives that generate demand and create new opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales Effectiveness &amp;amp; Conversion: &lt;/strong&gt;Analyse outreach, engagement and conversion data to continuously improve targeting, messaging, prospecting methods and lead quality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CRM &amp;amp; Pipeline Discipline: &lt;/strong&gt;Maintain accurate CRM data and account intelligence, providing clear visibility of prospecting activity, lead progression and pipeline development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance &amp;amp; Impact: &lt;/strong&gt;Deliver against defined lead-generation and pipeline objectives, measuring success through qualified leads, opportunities created, pipeline progression and contribution to new-logo growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will being to Ensono&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 8+ years of experience in business development, new logo acquisition, sales, or sales support within the IT/managed services industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of supporting successful client acquisition and building net-new pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience analysing sales performance and market data to inform BD strategy and improve conversion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate research and market intelligence into actionable go-to-market plays.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting partnership development and structured pursuit cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of managed services, cloud solutions, and IT infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication, proposal creation, and stakeholder-engagement skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage CRM hygiene and support process improvements to accelerate BD effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic thinker with the ability to identify whitespace opportunities and influence decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated, results-oriented, and able to operate independently and collaboratively in a fast-moving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel when needed for client and stakeholder engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we can offer you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a people-first business, people are at the heart of everything we do here. We offer our associates a safe environment where learning, knowledge sharing, and open communication is encouraged. Whether at one of the internal social events, competency meet-ups, hackathons or as part of one or more of our global Community Groups, such as Beautiful Brains (for the neurodiverse and curious), HERO (helping to education regarding orientation), E-Vets (Ensono veteran community) and many more, we strive to ensure that everyone feels welcome, included, and valued. Additionally, our standard benefits include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive base with uncapped commission&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to work from a range of flexible locations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prestigious sales and broader team recognition with Annual Presidents Club&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Starting with 27 days annual leave (plus bank holidays) – accruing to 30&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1/2 day leave on your birthday&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sabbatical options at 5 &amp;amp; 10 years&#39; service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 days study leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous company pension&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private healthcare for you and your family&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Payroll giving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced paternity and maternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity appreciation program incentive plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life and income protection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additional perks such as discounted gym memberships, cycle scheme, EAP and more.&amp;nbsp; If this all sounds great, we’d love to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: Stoke-on-Trent ST1&lt;br&gt;Training Period: Will be conducted Monday to Friday, 9am to 6pm for the first four weeks&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working hours: 40 hours per week, 5 days out of any 7 (8 hours a day, between 7:50am - 2am)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remuneration Package&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Up to&amp;nbsp;20%&amp;nbsp;annual&amp;nbsp;company bonus and u&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;nsociable hours allowance, when applicable&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Office-based for the first 4 months (probation and training period) - this will allow you to get to know the team, soak up crucial knowledge and benefit from face to face support whilst learning the role!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hybrid working (2 days in the office) available after successful completion of probation period&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Providing the best in class service to our players needs lots of work.&amp;nbsp;Your energy and passion will be put to good use, and the more you give, the more you’ll get in return.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;LiveScore Group is home to LiveScore, LiveScore Bet and Virgin Bet, three of the most exciting brands in the sports and gaming industries today. We are passionate and excited about what we do in the Sports Media, Gaming and Betting sector and are proud of the high ratings we have achieved. We live our values, aiming to enhance and increase the enjoyment of sport through innovative products and immersive experiences. Trust is important in how we work, ensuring we are a collaborative unit who holds each other accountable. Relentlessly ambitious in everything we do, we embrace change and understand that failure is part of success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We use our platform for positive social change and work to build a company our employees are proud to work for. We have a long-term commitment to diversity and inclusion. Our I.D.E.A (Inclusion, Diversity, Equality, Awareness) Forum is critical to our business and is embedded in our organisational structure to support a sense of belonging for everyone and to create a culture that allows all employees to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We know a job description can often deter an applicant who does not believe they match 100% of our requirements. If you are interested in this position and have relevant experience, then we would still love to hear from you.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Act as a first point of contact for our players providing them with a resolution to their sporting or gaming query. Sports betting happens quickly; in this role we will expect you to think fast and react even faster.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Try to resolve everything, first time, every time. With complex issues, you should ascertain urgency and follow the appropriate next steps in line with the department guidelines, escalating issues to the right department or Service Lead where appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time is of the essence. You’d need to manage all tasks in an efficient and timely manner. If you follow the escalation procedure, keep track and see it through resolution, too.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Numbers are important. We need tip-top mathematicians to provide our players with transactional advice on banking, deposits, withdrawals, pricing and calculation of bet settlements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The art of conversation. You’d need to communicate effectively and efficiently with players, colleagues, Service Leads and the Management Team to ensure delivery of business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hit the spot. Our department KPIs need to be met (or exceeded) and so we ask that you’re fast, efficient and that you get it right first time to thrill our players and reduce duplicate contacts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge is power - Keep on top of sports, as well as our other products and tools, to ensure you’re keeping up with our players, and with the business and department’s strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with other departments, take part in projects, and attend meetings at other locations as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have fun, making fun – Contribute to, and promote, a positive working environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become a constant, positive role model and drive to inspire others to have fun whilst working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be proactive and demonstrate Real Time Resource Management awareness maintaining service levels and efficiencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deflect Operator Complaints by handling 2&lt;sup&gt;nd&lt;/sup&gt; line escalations and finding positive solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a flexible attitude towards shift patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills, Knowledge and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A key understanding of the business and department OKRs with a determination to achieve and exceed targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A technical problem solver with a focus on helping develop internal functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ability to bring outstanding issues to a resolution, building key relationships across the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaise with key stakeholders raising critical issues and reduce the customer propensity to contact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To escalate and help guide company decisions through sharing voice of the player feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A problem solver whilst showing commercial awareness for each player.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An expert in the group marketing initiatives and internal functions and processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To be able to resolve complex queries and show a commitment in helping guide the CS Advisor group.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain &amp;amp; exceed the internal QA score going above and beyond for each customer contact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An expert in handling multiple Live Chat, email &amp;amp; social media&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding customer handling skills, as well as oral and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An investigative approach whilst fact-finding to guarantee first contact resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent PC skills, who is an expert with Excel and the web.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fast and accurate typing skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sports knowledge &amp;amp; a passion for sports is essential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What can we offer?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company Performance bonus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid working for all staff with flexible working opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private Healthcare scheme + Employee Enhanced Assistance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced Family Leave - Maternity, Shared Parental &amp;amp; Adoption Leave: up to 6 months at full pay and 6 months at half pay. Paternity leave: up to 4 weeks at full pay&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidised gym membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life Assurance (x3 salary)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributory Pension Plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Daily snacks, quality coffee, soft drinks and regular socials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Avetta is building the largest global community of hiring clients and suppliers that are Ready to Work. Its unified platform streamlines compliance, prequalification, safety and performance benchmarking in a single, integrated experience. Trusted by 360,000 businesses across more than 120 countries, Avetta blends AI-driven insights and human expertise to close risk gaps and strengthen supplier reliability so projects start on time, risks are managed proactively and operations scale with certainty.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SUMMARY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Account Executive will play a key role in expanding Avetta&#39;s footprint by driving new business with mid-market and enterprise clients in the EMEA region. This role requires a consultative sales approach - listening, uncovering challenges, and crafting solutions that deliver measurable impact. The ideal candidate has a track record of closing mid to high-value SaaS deals, managing complex sales cycles, and meeting revenue targets. This includes experience working with large multinational companies, engaging complex buying committees and buyer journeys, and applying proven methodologies such as MEDDPICC - &amp;nbsp;with exposure to Challenger selling principles - to drive success. At Level I, the Account Executive operates with active guidance from sales leadership, building proficiency in Avetta&#39;s sales motion, methodology, and buyer dynamics. The Account Executive owns the primary relationship with prospective Avetta clients before and during their buyer journey. Once a prospect becomes a client, the Account Executive continues to manage and service the relationship until the account is fully established, at which point it transitions to the Account Management Team for ongoing support and expansion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a hybrid role, working three days a week in our beautiful Maidenhead Office.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive new client acquisition by identifying and engaging mid-market and enterprise prospects, building relationships with key decision-makers, and developing strategies to generate business opportunities and grow Avetta&#39;s sales pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the full sales cycle - from prospecting and qualification through presentations, negotiations, and signed agreements - while partnering with internal teams to ensure client needs are met.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply MEDDPICC to qualify and progress opportunities, developing proficiency in the methodology with coaching from leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a weekly emphasis on business development initiatives to ensure consistent progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistently work toward revenue goals while keeping a well-managed pipeline in Salesforce, and provide clear, timely forecasts and insights to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with an assigned Sales Development Representative to execute targeted prospecting strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Avetta at industry trade shows and engage in networking activities to build relationships and promote Avetta&#39;s solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct comprehensive Avetta Overview Presentations and Product Demonstrations online.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel regularly to client sites and key accounts to facilitate in-person meetings, plus sales events, conferences, and other client-facing engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide essential support to new clients during the initial launch phase and throughout the first ninety days, with a focus on maximizing revenue and ensuring client success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively participate in weekly 1-on-1 meetings and team calls to stay aligned with Avetta&#39;s goals and strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend additional trainings, meetings, and seminars as required, and adhere to other duties assigned to contribute to Avetta&#39;s success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IDEAL EXPERIENCE, EDUCATION &amp;amp; TRAINING:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2 - 5 years of SaaS sales experience, including exposure to both mid-market and enterprise-level SaaS sales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with a structured sales methodology such as MEDDPICC; exposure to Challenger selling a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling safety-related products or services, working with contractors, working in procurement, or working in an industry that Avetta has current customers is considered a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational skills - this role requires significant travel, meeting coordination, and RFP/RFI/RFQ response management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior communication - exceptional interpersonal and written communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong public speaking - ability to confidently present to groups, maintain engagement, and communicate complex topics with clarity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated - able to set and pursue goals with guidance and support from sales leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical understanding - able to grasp and communicate SaaS software functionality and demonstrate product capabilities to clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ethical - embodies Avetta&#39;s core values of honesty and integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OTHER DESIRED TRAITS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent time management, technical proficiency (CRM/Salesforce), problem-solving, attention to detail, and adaptability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
